						RUNNING 	




							
About the Club

The Lavasa Running Club is a student-driven initiative under the Department of Physical Education & Sports at CHRIST (Deemed to be University), Pune Lavasa Campus. Founded with the vision of promoting holistic well-being, the club encourages students, staff, and the local community to embrace running as a way of life. Offering an inclusive platform for beginners and seasoned runners alike, the club organizes weekly runs across Lavasa’s scenic terrain, endurance training sessions, fitness awareness campaigns, and participation in marathons and city runs. Through consistent practice, leadership opportunities, and peer mentoring, the Running Club nurtures discipline, resilience, teamwork, and a lifelong commitment to physical and mental fitness.

