						LAVASA MUSIC ACADEMY	




							
About the Club

Lavasa Music Academy, also known as the CHRIST Music School, is a vibrant creative space where music serves as a bridge across diverse interests and experience levels. The academy is dedicated to making musical learning accessible to students, staff, and guests, regardless of prior exposure. Offering structured courses in Piano, Drums, and Acoustic Guitar, the club supports both beginners and experienced musicians through hands-on learning and collaborative performances. Weekly sessions held every Saturday emphasize skill development, personal expression, and emotional well-being. Beyond training, the academy enriches campus culture through recitals, workshops, ensemble performances, and open mic sessions. By fostering creativity, teamwork, and leadership, Lavasa Music Academy celebrates the transformative power of music and builds meaningful connections within the campus community.

